This repository is a clone of Diskghost at commit 0034d79, with its history
kept and a remote named "upstream" for later updates.

What comes from Diskghost:

- crates/diskghost-core: the scanning, MFT and snapshot engine. Changed in these
  places, with the evidence in docs/benchmarks:
  - src/mft.rs, to fix folders counted twice (2026-11-core-acceptance.md).
  - src/walk.rs, to list directories through the kernel's own call, and to record
    which ones could not be listed (src/tree.rs, ScanTree::unlistable_dirs)
    (2026-11-speed-and-footprint.md).
  - src/snapshot.rs, Snapshot::folders_only, to keep older scans small (same report).
- app/src-tauri/src/helper.rs: adapted from Diskghost's gui/src-tauri/src/helper.rs.
  It takes its instructions differently, for safety; see the top of that file.

Diskghost's GUI, command line tool, duplicate finder and delete features are not
part of Diskly. The core library still contains its delete functions, because it
is kept as it is. Diskly does not call them, and a test enforces that.

Everything else in this repository was written for Diskly.
